00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.070 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  sever donetsk has been under fire for  weeks but it remains a ukrainian holdout  russia encircled the city days ago and  is using a familiar strategy of  submission through bombardment  like mariupol citizens are taking cover  in an industrial plant ukrainian  officials say about 800 are hiding in  the nitrogen facility along with an  unknown number of soldiers  invading forces have seized almost every  other part of luhansk in eastern ukraine  where russia is concentrating its  offensive  russia announced it destroyed a large  cache of ukrainian weapons and military  equipment in the east monday  ukrainian police in the donetsk region  recorded images of civilian buildings  hit by missiles as they were in the  community imploring people to leave  at that moment i had a feeling that the  building was made of rubber everything  was moving  russian tactics particularly in harkief  amount to war crimes according to  amnesty international many of these  strikes were  launched using  cluster munitions which are widely  banned  as well as other  indiscriminate weapons ukrainian  soldiers the report says have positioned  themselves in residential areas  violating international humanitarian  laws and drawing fire but  this  in no way justifies the relentless and  discriminated shelling of the city by  russian forces  the war over ukraine's sovereignty is  nearing its fourth month  krystal gamansen global news london

